  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Investing for impact against HIV - An effective and efficient response to HIV in Tunisia - Tunisia (01-Jan-2017-31-Dec-2018)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tunisia, HIV, Office National de la Famille et de la Population de la R&#xe9;publique de Tunisie (ONFP)This program has the following goals: New infections are reduced by 50 percent by 2018.  The mortality rate among PLHIV is reduced by 60 percent by 2018. The objectives of this program are: Objective 1: By 2018, at least 80 percent of each at-risk population benefiting from the programs will adopt safer behavior (SWs, MSM, people who inject drugs)..  Objective 2: By 2018, at least 80 percent of each vulnerable population (prisoners, migrants, clients/partners of key populations) will adopt safer behavior..  Objective 3: By 2018, at least 50 percent of vulnerable people aged 30-44 will adopt safer behavior with regard to STIs and HIV..  Objective 4: At least 60 percent of people seeking advice for an STI will adopt preventive behavior..  Objective 5: By 2018, the rate of MTCT of HIV will have been reduced by 90 percent among children born to HIV-positive mothers..  Objective 6: By 2018, at least 60 percent of health care facilities will apply standard precautionary measures for blood transfusion safety and HIV exposure accidents..  Objective 7: By 2018, at least 80 percent of PLHIV (children and adults) diagnosed will survive 12 months following commencement of ART.</narrative>
  </description>
